---
description: Rules for building responsive UI from Figma via MCP
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

# Figma → code

- Figma MCP output is a reference, not final code. Convert absolute positioning and fixed px widths into flex/grid layouts.
- Build section by section. Never generate a whole page at once.

# Responsive

- Mobile-first CSS. Breakpoints: md = 768px, lg = 1024px, xl = 1440px.
- No fixed widths/heights for layout; use %, max-width, flex, grid, clamp().
- When given tablet/mobile Figma links for an existing section: first list the differences per breakpoint, then modify the EXISTING component. Never create a separate mobile/tablet component or file.

```css
/* ❌ BAD: desktop-first, fixed layout width */
.benefits { display: flex; width: 1280px; }
@media (max-width: 768px) { .benefits { flex-direction: column; } }

/* ✅ GOOD: mobile-first, fluid */
.benefits { display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); max-width: var(--content-max); }
@media (min-width: 1024px) { .benefits { grid-template-columns: 0.75fr 1fr; } }
```

# Components & tokens

- Before creating any component, search /components (or src/components) and reuse it.
- All colors, spacing, radii and fonts come from tokens (tokens.css / tailwind config). No hardcoded hex or px values for these.
- Use image/icon assets returned by the Figma MCP; don't invent placeholders.

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
.card { background: #1741b3; border-radius: 36px; padding: 40px; }

/* ✅ GOOD */
.card { background: var(--color-blue); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: var(--space-10); }
```
